# ── CONTENT DIRECTORIES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `docs/` and `knowledge/` are excluded to keep the build context lean, and
# then selectively re-included below. That is not a cosmetic split: some of
# what lives under those paths is documentation, and some of it is
# APPLICATION CONTENT that a service reads at build time or at runtime.
# Excluding all of it produced two failures on 2026-08-10, one loud and one
# silent:
#
#  · `apps/web`'s build reads `docs/learning/` to generate the strategy
#    catalogue and lesson pages. Without it, `next build` fails outright with
#    "Failed to collect page data for /learning/strategy/[id]" — the web image
#    could not be built at all.
#
#  · `services/sentinel` builds its citation corpus by scanning
#    `docs/Trading Books`, `docs/product-architecture`, `docs/handbook`,
#    `knowledge/`, `knowledge-base/` and `agents/` (see
#    si.config.ts DEFAULT_CORPUS_ROOTS). This one is SILENT: the image builds
#    fine, the container starts fine, and the corpus is empty. Sentinel's
#    citation guarantee is structural — `VerdictBuilder.knowledge()` cannot be
#    called without citations, and the cross-checker DROPS uncited verdicts —
#    so an empty corpus does not raise an error. It makes Sentinel
#    permanently silent, which is a designed and normal-looking outcome. The
#    flagship premium feature would have shipped as a no-op with no error
#    anywhere.
#
# Adding a corpus root in si.config.ts therefore means adding it here too.

docs
!docs/learning
!docs/product-architecture
!docs/handbook
# ~30 MB of PDFs, and by far the largest thing in any image. It earns its place:
# these 14 books ARE Sentinel's knowledge base, and without them the corpus has
# no `book`-tier documents to cite. If image size becomes a problem, move them
# to object storage and give the scanner a remote root — do not simply drop
# them here, because the failure is silent.
!docs/Trading Books

knowledge
!knowledge/sentinel-learning
# The engineering vault is a corpus root at `vault` authority tier, and is also
# what the admin Knowledge Workspace serves.
!knowledge/**/*.md
!knowledge/_INDEX.md

# `knowledge-base/` (market-concept ontology) and `agents/` are corpus roots
# too, and are deliberately NOT excluded anywhere in this file.

# Superseded code (CLAUDE.md Rule 1). The corpus scanner skips it by name as
# well, so that a design that was explicitly abandoned cannot teach the
# reasoning engine.
archive

infra/k8s
infra/terraform
